\[
\frac{dV}{dt}=Q_{\mathrm{in}}-Q_{\mathrm{out}}
=3.2\times10^{-3}-2.5\times10^{-3}
=7.0\times10^{-4}\,\mathrm{m^3\,s^{-1}}
\]
The tank volume is increasing, so the amount of water in the tank is not steady.

Use mass flow rate:
\[
\dot m=\rho Av
\]
\[
v=\frac{\dot m}{\rho A}
=\frac{0.72}{(900)(4.0\times10^{-4})}
=2.0\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}
\]
Treating \(Q=Av\) as constant across sections requires constant density. Mass flow rate is the conserved quantity for general steady flow.
